PORT=5999
HOST=0.0.0.0
MCP_PUBLIC_URL=https://mcp.example.com
# Base64-encoded random secret, at least 32 bytes
JWT_SECRET=
MCP_DEFAULT_USER_EMAIL=demo@example.com
MCP_DEFAULT_USER_PASSWORD=
STORAGE_PATH=./data/app.sqlite
MCP_DEFAULT_USER_ID=demo-user

# Gmail API access: use a refresh token for long-running deployments.
# Required OAuth scope: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly
GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=
GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# Optional short-lived access token for local smoke tests; takes precedence over refresh-token auth.
GMAIL_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# HMAC key used to persist only a digest of each user's username+agent@gmail.com recipient.
# Generate at least 32 random bytes; changing it invalidates stored recipient digests.
AGENT_RECIPIENT_HMAC_SECRET=

# Google sign-in and per-user Gmail read-only access.
# Configure the OAuth web client with this exact authorised redirect URI:
# https://your-host.example/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://mcp.example.com/auth/google/callback
# Base64-encoded random 32-byte key for AES-256-GCM encryption of per-user Google refresh tokens.
GOOGLE_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
# Independent HMAC key for deriving internal pseudonymous user IDs from Google issuer + sub.
IDENTITY_HMAC_SECRET=

# Privacy notice: all fields below are required and non-empty at startup.
# Controller identity and contact details are deployment-specific; do not publish guesses.
GDPR_CONTROLLER_NAME=
GDPR_CONTROLLER_ADDRESS=
GDPR_CONTROLLER_EMAIL=
GDPR_PRIVACY_CONTACT_EMAIL=
SERVICE_HOSTING_COUNTRY=Finland
AI_SERVICE_DESTINATION_COUNTRY=Configure per deployment; users may choose providers in different countries
GDPR_PURPOSES=To provide read-only email routing from Gmail to the AI service that the user has explicitly configured through this MCP service. This includes Google sign-in, locating messages addressed to the user's +agent alias, presenting message metadata, and retrieving message bodies only when requested by the authorised AI client. The service does not send or modify email.
GDPR_LAWFUL_BASIS=Consent under GDPR Article 6(1)(a): the user chooses to sign in with Google, authorises read-only Gmail access, and configures an AI client to request this email-routing service. The controller must ensure consent is freely given, specific, informed, unambiguous, and can be withdrawn.
GDPR_RETENTION=Service account data, recipient HMAC digest, encrypted Google refresh token, and associated MCP authorisation records are deleted after 15 consecutive days without a successful MCP tool call. They are also deleted when the user completes Google-verified account deletion. The discovered +agent address is held in process memory for up to five minutes. Message headers and bodies are not persisted by the connector; they are fetched from Gmail for each request and returned to the authorised AI client. Hosting logs, Google, AI providers, and backups may have separate retention periods and must be configured or documented separately.
GDPR_RECIPIENTS=Google LLC and relevant Google entities for Google Identity and Gmail API processing; the service hosting provider and its infrastructure subprocessors; and the AI service provider selected and configured by the user, which receives message data returned by this MCP service. The controller must identify the actual hosting and AI providers and review their terms and subprocessors for this deployment.
GDPR_INTERNATIONAL_TRANSFERS=Google may process Gmail and identity data in countries around the world. This service processes requested data in the hosting country configured in SERVICE_HOSTING_COUNTRY, then transmits matching message metadata and, when requested, message content to the AI provider configured by the user, whose destination is configured in AI_SERVICE_DESTINATION_COUNTRY. This may involve transfers outside the EEA. The controller must identify the actual countries, verify the relevant transfer mechanisms and safeguards (such as an adequacy decision or applicable Standard Contractual Clauses), and provide any required transfer information; this template does not assert that a specific safeguard applies.
GDPR_SUPERVISORY_AUTHORITY=Office of the Data Protection Ombudsman (Tietosuojavaltuutetun toimisto), Lintulahdenkuja 4, 00530 Helsinki, Finland. Website: https://tietosuoja.fi/en/home
# Optional: set only if a Data Protection Officer has been appointed.
GDPR_DPO_CONTACT=
